---
import Layout from '@/layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout title="No path found" description="404. The planner checked, and there is genuinely no route to this page.">
  <section class="shell-read wrap">
    <p class="eyebrow">Error 404</p>
    <h1>No path found.</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      In SkyScout this exact result was once correct. A* returned no path, I assumed the planner was
      broken, and a connected-components check showed the goal really was cut off. The empty answer was
      the right answer.
    </p>
    <p class="lede">This time it is simpler. There is no page at that address.</p>

    <pre class="term mono">planner: A*
goal:    unreachable
check:   connected components -> goal not in free space
result:  no path (correct)</pre>

    <div class="btns">
      <a href="/" class="btn btn-primary">Back to the start</a>
      <a href="/missions/" class="btn btn-ghost">Missions</a>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>

<style>
  .wrap { padding: 10rem 1.5rem 4rem; }
  h1 { font-size: clamp(2.5rem, 8vw, 4.5rem); font-weight: 600; letter-spacing: -0.04em; margin: 0.6rem 0 1.5rem; }
  .lede { margin: 0 0 1.25rem; color: var(--ink-soft); font-size: 1.0625rem; line-height: 1.65; }
  .term {
    margin: 2rem 0;
    padding: 1.5rem;
    background: var(--surface-solid);
    border: 1px solid var(--hairline);
    border-left: 2px solid var(--accent);
    border-radius: 1rem;
    font-size: 0.8125rem;
    line-height: 1.8;
    color: var(--ink-soft);
    overflow-x: auto;
  }
  .btns { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 0.75rem; }
</style>
